    "['set routing-options forwarding-table export [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip load-sharing per-packet', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip load-sharing per-packet', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nip load-sharing per-packet\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command `set routing-options forwarding-table export load-balance` enables per-packet load balancing across multiple equal-cost paths in the forwarding table.\\n- In Cisco IOS, `ip load-sharing per-packet` achieves the same functionality by enabling per-packet load balancing (as opposed to the default per-destination load balancing).\\n- Note that this command would be configured under the global configuration mode in Cisco.\", 'trans_template': 'ip load-sharing per-packet'}]]": 1
